1|[[1d4]] Beggars, thieves, or urchins: Beggar, thief, or urchin begs for money, and curses the player-character if nothing is given.
2-5|[[1d4]] Beggars or thieves (plus 1 lurking nearby): Beggar or thief shams drunkenness to bump into the player-character and try to rob him.
6-7|1 Beggar, thief, or urchin (plus 1 lurking nearby): Beggar, thief, or urchin tries to con the player-character. Roll [[1d20]] on the encounter matrix list for the disguise of the con-man. Re-roll on a result of 9.
8-14|[[4d4]] Beggars or thieves: Beggar or thief attempts to mug the player-characters.
15-16|[[1d4]] Beggars or thieves: Beggar or thief is in trouble with his guild and asks the player-characters for help.
17-18|[[1d10]] Beggars or thieves: Beggar or thief approaches the player-characters to go on a special mission (see Table 29 to determine the mission).
19|[[1d10]] Thieves (plus [[1d10]] lurking nearby): Player-characters accidentally witness a thief-gang ceremony. If they are noticed (base chance 30%), the gang attempts to kill or capture the player-characters.
20|1 Beggar, thief, or urchin: Beggar, thief, or urchin recognizes the player-character. Roll [[1d20]]: on 1-14, he is mistaken; on 15-20, he is correct.